From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristjan Sillmann <kristjan.h.s@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi-watcher-reset

vic-switchboard WifiWatcher: reset the failed-autoconnect count whenever the robot is on WiFi,
so only consecutive failures (5) restart wpa_supplicant + connman. wire-pod's WiFi switch
(connmanctl connect) makes each switchboard attempt fail InProgress; the count never reset, so
every 3rd-5th switch restarted connman mid-switch (robot log 2026-11-07 19:58:12, sudo by net).
Logs my-vector.WifiWatcherReset.
---
 platform/switchboard/switchboardd/wifiWatcher.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/platform/switchboard/switchboardd/wifiWatcher.cpp b/platform/switchboard/switchboardd/wifiWatcher.cpp
index 5272e52a..421287bb 100644
--- a/platform/switchboard/switchboardd/wifiWatcher.cpp
+++ b/platform/switchboard/switchboardd/wifiWatcher.cpp
@@ -59,6 +59,12 @@ void WifiWatcher::ConnectIfNoWifi() {
   if((wifiState.connState == Anki::Wifi::WiFiConnState::CONNECTED) ||
     (wifiState.connState == Anki::Wifi::WiFiConnState::ONLINE)) {
     // robot is on wifi, so carry on!
+    // my-vector: count only consecutive failed autoconnects. A WiFi switch by another tool (connmanctl connect)
+    // makes each attempt fail InProgress; never reset, those added up to a wpa_supplicant/connman restart.
+    if(_connectErrorCount > 0) {
+      Log::Write("WifiWatcher: on wifi again, my-vector.WifiWatcherReset of %d failed autoconnects", _connectErrorCount);
+      _connectErrorCount = 0;
+    }
     return;
   }
 
